From e1e02edf992137ee2279d1a3cd5d226547330f3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dameng <dameng@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:37:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] EDBT v4 B7 (Phase B2): measured operator-trace rows only with
 actual_reads; operator wall/rows sidecar; mechanism proxy builder

The pack validator contract requires every attribution_level=measured_per_execution
row in operator_segment_trace.csv to carry actual_reads. The B5 emission wrote such
rows for ALL scans with actual_reads empty whenever the query referenced a
(table,column) more than once (unique-scan rule) -> the measured smoke bundle failed
validation (25-error cap; the whole non-unique row class).

Fix: operator_segment_trace.csv now receives measured rows ONLY for unique scans
(attribution always reliable); every scan's measured wall_ns/rows_in/rows_out move
to a new attribution-free sidecar benchmark_operator_wall_rows.csv (unique_scan
column documents the rule). measured_segment_access.csv (per-segment deltas, all
segments) is unchanged.

Also versions experiments/edbt_v4/build_mechanism_proxy.py (B2-4 downstream half:
per-cycle counter deltas + tiered logical access proxy).
